  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: \n\nUpper level ridge continues to move back west and south over the \ndesert SW, effectively cutting of the monsoon moisture feed, \nmeaning storm chances will continue to wind down through the \nweekend. Friday, and into the weekend the upper level flow will \nchange from being southerly to more drier southwest flow, bringing\nstorm chances to an end after Sunday. With the drying trend, \ntemperatures are set to gradually warm through the weekend with \nhigh pressure in control, and cloud cover dissipating. A heat \nadvisory is in effect for northern Nevada, as high temperature \nwill range between 95 to 103 degrees each day. Models have had a \nchange since yesterday for the long term, models runs prior have \nhinted at a return to monsoonal flow over Nevada by the end of the\nmonth. Solutions today now show the upper ridge moving farther \nwest setting up over the Great Basin and lower Colorado river \nvalley. Models then show the ridge strengthening with height \nreaching 600 daM, which is very strong. If this solutions set \nholds, the monsoon will stay east of NV and very warm temperatures\nwill persist through next week. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n \nThere is high confidence for decreasing thunderstorm chances each\nafternoon, eventually ending by Sunday afternoon.\n\nThere High confidence in the potential for warming temperatures \nthrough the weekend. With a Heat Advisory in effect for Friday.\n\nThere is low confidence in the evolution of the upper air pattern\nafter Wednesday early as model consistency in possible solutions \nis low.",
